@meta
id: 19-13
title: Keep your place
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: location-list, cdo
par: 145
minutes: 8
vscode: two searches in one panel, the first one gone
vimrc: set hidden smartcase
open: README.md

@brief
Three `FIXME` comments under `src`. Each needs reading: the ones whose
ticket is closed go, the one still open stays. ORD-290 is closed.
ORD-402 is open. Load them into the location list and start walking.

The first FIXME asks for a rename that is now safe to do:
`PaymentProducer.refundIssued` becomes `refundCompleted`, in the
producer, both providers and the order provider's test. That is a
`:vimgrep` and a `:cdo`, and running `:vimgrep` replaces the quickfix
list. It does not touch the location list. When the rename is done,
`:lne` picks the FIXME walk up exactly where you left it, in the same
window.

Do the rename when the FIXME tells you to. Delete the two closed
FIXMEs. Leave the open one. The event type `RefundIssuedEvent` is a
type name, not the method, and keeps its name.

@keys
| `:lvimgrep` `:lne` | a walk that belongs to this window |
| `:vimgrep` `:cdo` | a job that uses the quickfix list, and replaces it |

@hints
`:lvimgrep /FIXME/ **/*.ts` lands on the first one, in the order
provider. Read it, `dd`, `:w`.
--
`:vimgrep /refundIssued/ **/*.ts` and
`:cdo s/refundIssued/refundCompleted/g | update`. The quickfix list is
now the rename. The location list is still the FIXMEs.
--
`:lne`. The next FIXME is ORD-402 and stays. `:lne` again: ORD-290,
`dd`, `:wq`.

@solution
    :lvimgrep /FIXME/ **/*.ts<Enter>  dd :w<Enter>
    :vimgrep /refundIssued/ **/*.ts<Enter>  :cdo s/refundIssued/refundCompleted/g | update<Enter>
    :lne<Enter>  :lne<Enter>  dd :wq<Enter>

Two lists, two jobs, and neither trod on the other. The walk needed a
human at every stop, so it went in the location list, which is the
list for things you are doing by hand in this window. The rename was
mechanical and global, so it went through quickfix, which any command
may overwrite at any time.

Notice that `:lne` still knew it was on entry one of three, and that
entry three still pointed at the right line even though the `:cdo` had
rewritten a line in the same file. Both lists are live: edits shift
their entries, and each remembers its own position.

The other way to survive a replaced quickfix list is to get the old one
back, which lesson 18 covers. Having two lists is simpler when you know
in advance that you will be interrupted.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);
    // FIXME ORD-290: rename PaymentProducer.refundIssued to refundCompleted once the ledger consumer is live
    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: order.id, receipt: 'pending' });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);
    await this.paymentProducer.refundCompleted({ paymentId: order.id, receipt: 'pending' });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const paymentProducer = stub<PaymentProducer>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService, paymentProducer);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).sendRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
    expect(paymentProducer.refundIssued).toHaveBeenCalled();
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
